# Drift events: each violates the php-fpm SBoB and MUST fire the mapped rule.
# These are the PHP2Shell post-exploit behaviors (CVE-2026-109618 /
# CVE-2026-109619 — see docs/php2shell-scenario.md): the point of the scenario
# is that the SBoB catches the BEHAVIOR after the in-worker RCE lands,
# regardless of which CVE was the entry vector.
#
#   execve /bin/sh -c ...              -> 100111 (SBoB drift: process ...)
#        CVE-2026-109618 in-worker RCE: the hijacked php-fpm worker spawns a
#        shell — php-fpm declares no shell exec, so /bin/sh is drift
#   open /var/tmp/.php2shell.php       -> 100121 (SBoB drift: file open ...)
#        the dropped webshell — /var/tmp is not in opens[] (web root is
#        read-only; session dir is the only declared write path)
#   connect 45.155.148.12:4444         -> 100131 (SBoB drift: connect ...)
#        CVE-2026-109619 stale-global-state RCE: the reverse shell / C2
#        callback — only internal memcache is declared egress
#   memfd_create (syscall 319)         -> 100163 (SBoB signature: ...)
#        the fileless variant: the in-worker payload stages itself in a
#        memfd instead of dropping the webshell (execution-from-memory
#        signature, node-scoped key, fires by default)

